          "text": "CHÊNG Hung-k'uei 鄭鴻逵 (T. 羽公) d. 1657, a native of Nan-an, Fukien, was a younger brother of Chêng Chih-lung [q. v.]. He became a military chü-jên in 1630 and in reward for his brother's naval operations against the Dutch was made lieutenant in the palace guards.",
